#question(title: [Fill in the blanks])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  Let $display({a_n})$ be a decreasing,
  bounded sequence.  \
  Assume $a_1 = 1$ and $a_n$ is never $0$.  \
  Let $m$ be the greatest lower bound of
  $display({a_n})$. \

  #v(.5em)

  For each of the statements below, find
  #strong[all] the values of $m$ that make
  the statement true.

  + IF
    #boxed[$display(#hide[$display(? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ?)$])$]
    THEN $display({1 \/ a_n})$ is bounded
  + IF
    #boxed[$display(#hide[$display(? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ?)$])$]
    THEN $display({1 \/ a_n})$ is increasing
  + IF
    #boxed[$display(#hide[$display(? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ?)$])$]
    THEN $display({sin a_n})$ is bounded
  + IF
    #boxed[$display(#hide[$display(? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ?)$])$]
    THEN $display({sin a_n})$ is decreasing
]
